{"full":"hf:k-mktr/candle-test-arena","spaceId":"k-mktr/candle-test-arena","name":"Candle Test Arena","source":"huggingface","description":"Evaluate LLM reasoning capabilities through the Candle Test","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["streamlit","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":4,"created":"2025-04-07T12:07:09.000Z","updated":"2025-04-08T19:22:28.000Z","license":"apache-2.0","runtime":"SLEEPING","appUrl":"https://k-mktr-candle-test-arena.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/k-mktr/candle-test-arena","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T10:59:44.287Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T10:59:44.287Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T10:59:44.287Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🕯️","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Streamlit application for evaluating LLM reasoning capabilities through a simple yet effective test that reveals fundamental limitations in how language models process context and avoid overfitting.","The Candle Test is a deceptively simple test that reveals a critical limitation in how LLMs process context and avoid overfitting. It was originally proposed by u/Everlier on Reddit as a way to demonstrate how even sophisticated language models can fall into the trap of overfitting to immediate context.","This implementation provides a user-friendly interface to run the test on various LLMs and analyze their performance, helping researchers and developers understand how different models handle context and reasoning."],"features":["🤔 Correctly understanding a basic fact (candles get shorter as they burn)","🧠 Holding this fact in context","🎯 But then failing to avoid overfitting when presented with a riddle that seems to match the context","Comprehensive Testing:","Test any OpenAI-compatible model"],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/k-mktr/candle-test-arena/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5f6e29a5919bfebdc08ed63826c91a1c20d3f268e8c3f0102bbc2d7cc38c